---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HomeProject from '../components/HomeProject.astro';
import ForecastChart from '../components/ForecastChart.astro';
import portrait from '../../assets/ashmit-portrait.png';
import { affiliation } from '../data/profile';
---
<Layout>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="introduction" id="about">
      <div id="background">
        <p class="affiliation">{affiliation}, class of 2027</p>
        <h1>I build AI systems, from multi-agent workflows to the pipelines and platforms research runs on.</h1>
        <p>I graduate in May 2027. I'm looking for AI and ML engineering roles, and applying to MSc and PhD programs in computer science.</p>
        <p class="hero-tools" aria-label="Languages and frameworks">Python, TypeScript, Kotlin, Swift · PyTorch, FastAPI, React, SwiftUI</p>
        <div class="hero-links"><Fragment set:html={'<!--email_off--><a href="mailto:asm8879@nyu.edu">asm8879@nyu.edu</a><!--/email_off-->'} /><a href="https://github.com/Ansester">GitHub</a></div>
      </div>
      <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Ashmit Mukherjee" width={160} height={160} densities={[1, 2]} format="webp" loading="eager" />
    </header>

    <section class="home-section" id="research" aria-labelledby="group-decisions">
      <h2 id="group-decisions">Group decisions and AI advice</h2>
      <HomeProject title="AI advice and cooperation" href="/work/human-ai-collaboration/">
        <p>In the Social Dynamics Lab, I built the platform for our experiments and lead its development. Each player can get a private recommendation from an AI adviser. We vary whether the advisers talk to each other first, then trace how players respond. So far I have tested it with model players across three games.</p>
        <Fragment slot="notes">
          <p>Social Dynamics Lab</p>
          <p>Faculty mentors · Professors <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=GAxIreYAAAAJ">Benjamin Rosche</a> and <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=9lTiKjwAAAAJ">Hanan Salam</a></p>
          <p>2026 to present</p>
        </Fragment>
      </HomeProject>
      <HomeProject title="Forecasting the effect of punishment on group earnings" href="/work/synthetic-pilot-lab/">
        <p>For my capstone, I asked whether language models could forecast what punishment does to a group’s earnings. Claude Haiku 4.5 and the human experts both expected a small gain. Across the 20 game designs, groups earned less on average with punishment. The three Claude models and both crowds beat a no-change guess by under a point. GPT-5 had more error than the no-change guess. The original study’s elastic net beat it by 2.6.</p>
        <ForecastChart compact />
        <Fragment slot="notes">
          <p>Independent capstone</p>
          <p>Advisers · Professors <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=9lTiKjwAAAAJ">Hanan Salam</a> and <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=GAxIreYAAAAJ">Benjamin Rosche</a></p>
          <p>2026 to present</p>
          <p><a href="/research/group-earnings-forecast-note.pdf">My forecast study (PDF)</a></p>
        </Fragment>
      </HomeProject>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="protein">
      <h2 id="protein">Protein language models</h2>
      <HomeProject id="manuscript" title="Bio-LoRA for protein language models" href="/work/protein-language-models/">
        <p>Bio-LoRA uses the chemistry of amino acids to give protein models a better starting point for training. My part was the pipeline for identifying signal peptides and predicting where they are cut. On a separate test of mutation effects, Bio-LoRA reached a rank correlation of 0.45, compared with 0.43 for standard LoRA and 0.55 for full fine-tuning.</p>
        <Fragment slot="notes">
          <p>eBRAIN Lab</p>
          <p><a href="/work/protein-language-models/#manuscript">All nine authors share first authorship.</a></p>
          <p>Manuscript in revision, October 2026</p>
        </Fragment>
      </HomeProject>
      <HomeProject title="Biosynthesis paper database" href="/work/biosynthesis-paper-database/">
        <p>For a project on how AI systems retrieve methods from the biosynthesis literature, I wrote the pipeline that collected 139,011 paper records. About a third lacked abstracts. The lipid search also pulled in papers on cell signaling, a different question from how cells make lipids.</p>
        <Fragment slot="notes">
          <p>eBRAIN Lab</p>
          <p>Led by <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=USe518cAAAAJ">Minghao Shao</a>, with faculty lead Professor <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=xSR276UAAAAJ">Muhammad Shafique</a></p>
          <p>Fall 2026</p>
        </Fragment>
      </HomeProject>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="projects" aria-labelledby="software">
      <div class="section-heading" id="experience"><h2 id="software">Software and competitions</h2><a href="/work/">All projects</a></div>
      <HomeProject title="CSAW 2026 LLM CTF Attack Competition" href="/work/csaw-llm-ctf/">
        <p>My team, SegfaultObservers, took first place in the MENA region. I designed the six-agent system we used to work challenges in parallel and check each proposed flag.</p>
        <p slot="notes">November 2026</p>
      </HomeProject>
      <HomeProject title="FieldLens" href="/work/fieldlens/">
        <p>A local language model answers questions about vehicle incidents and links each statement to the camera or GPS record behind it.</p>
        <p slot="notes">Independent project, 2026</p>
      </HomeProject>
      <HomeProject title="RoomWise" href="/work/roomwise/">
        <p>Describe a chair in chat, swipe through listings, and compare how each one fits the same spot in your room. I made the browsing and room-preview interfaces.</p>
        <p slot="notes">With <a href="https://github.com/Aarz1401">Aadil Chasmawala</a>, 2026</p>
      </HomeProject>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
